cff-version: 1.2.0
title: langgraph-telemetry-fuzzer
message: >-
  If you use this software or its findings in your research, please cite it
  using these metadata.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Shah
    given-names: Himani
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/iamhimanishah/langgraph-telemetry-fuzzer
abstract: >-
  An evaluation harness that measures whether an incident-diagnosis agent
  abstains when its telemetry cannot support a conclusion. It injects
  reproducible corruption into observability data along four axes -- dropped
  datapoints, skewed timestamps, schema drift, and truncated windows -- and
  scores judgement (did the agent answer only when it should have?)
  separately from accuracy (was the answer right?). It also ships a guardrail
  layer that computes trust signals from telemetry alone, without access to
  ground truth, and so is deployable in production rather than only against
  a benchmark.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - agent evaluation
  - hallucination
  - calibration
  - abstention
  - observability
  - root cause analysis
  - AIOps
license: MIT
references:
  - type: dataset
    title: >-
      RCAEval: A Benchmark for Root Cause Analysis of Microservice Systems
    doi: 10.5281/zenodo.14590730
    notes: >-
      Used for the real-data worked example in scripts/run_real_incident.py.
